  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 墓\ntitle: grave; tomb\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 13\nradical: 土\nradicalNumber: 32\nonyomi: [ボ]\nkunyomi: [はか]\nquizOnyomi: []\nquizKunyomi: [はか]\ndistractors: [暮, 募, 川]\nquiz_exclusions: [埋, 石, 標, 塔]\n---\n\n# 墓 — grave; tomb\n\n**Strokes:** 13 · **Key (radical):** 土 (no. 32) · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n[墓](../words/墓.md) はか is a grave or tomb: a burial place or\nassociated structure. 日本国語大辞典 also includes the grave marker\nor gravestone among the things called はか.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** find the 莫-shaped upper\npart above [土](土.md), earth, and imagine a marker on the ground.\nThis is an invented scene for the present shape, not an account of\nhow the character originated.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Kind | Example or disposition |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ボ | on | 墳墓 ふんぼ, grave or tomb; recognition example, not linked practice. |\n| はか | kun | [墓](../words/墓.md) はか, grave or tomb; the existing article supports practice. |\n\nWeblio's Wiktionary section also lists モ as an on reading outside\nthe standard list. 字通 records おくつき and older dictionary forms;\nthese are retained as supplemental evidence, not added to practice.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [墓](../words/墓.md) はか - grave; tomb.\n- 墳墓 ふんぼ - grave; tomb.\n- 墓地 ぼち - cemetery; burial ground.\n\n## Notes\n\n- [暮](暮.md) shares much of the upper shape but concerns dusk or\n  livelihood; [募](募.md) concerns recruitment or solicitation.\n  Their readings and meanings must be learned in their own words.\n- [川](川.md) means a river or stream, not a burial place.\n- [埋](埋.md), bury or embed, receives a direct precaution for its\n  burial sense. A grave is a place or structure, not every act of\n  burying or filling.\n- [石](石.md), stone, receives a precaution because 墓 can also\n  refer to a grave marker or gravestone. Not every stone is a grave.\n- [標](標.md), mark or signpost, receives a precaution because a\n  grave marker is also a mark. Not every mark is a grave, and 標\n  does not independently mean grave.\n- [塔](塔.md), tower or pagoda, receives a precaution because some\n  stone towers serve as graves or grave markers. Not every tower\n  is a grave; an ordinary 供養塔 memorial tower is not generally\n  called a grave.\n- 浅墓 is a spelling of 浅はか あさはか, \"thoughtless\" or\n  \"shallow\"; JMdict marks this spelling as ateji. That whole-word\n  meaning is not an ordinary independent meaning of 墓.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project),\n2026-11-02 snapshot. Word families:\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project),\nentries 1514840, 1504630, 1584040, 1609030, 1168060, 1514900 and 1703230.\nSupplemental character and native-word senses:\n[Digital Daijisen, 日本国語大辞典 and 字通](https://kotobank.jp/word/墓);\n[Weblio's character sections](https://www.weblio.jp/content/墓).\nMarker and stone-tower senses: [標](https://kotobank.jp/word/標),\n[墓標](https://kotobank.jp/word/墓標), [石塔](https://kotobank.jp/word/石塔).\n",
